+## #2966 — Select a resident Agie quality for a 20 mm punch
+
+Use the existing Wire Contour condition field for both qualities. Keep AGIE_QN2 as the original Ra 0.30 µm selection. AGIE_BERCO_RA035 requests the documented Fine+ tuple from the MIT Agie Processor quality presets. Both condition rows require the existing preview gap and wire diameter. The normal project file preserves the selected condition.
+
+Qualify the alternate selection for a single closed punch on 20 mm cold die steel with Berco Cut 0.25 mm wire. A synthetic offline control job displayed Ra 0.35, Te 1.50 and Tkm 1.00 µm. The resident control selected T100 and four total passes using the same wire offsets as the original condition at this height. Use the measured maximum offset for geometry clearance. Leave unmeasured stock heights and other work cycles unsupported. A catalog pass estimate and the requested Ra cannot establish the achieved surface finish.
